    "title": "Richmond Refinery Cancer Risk Triples State Threshold, Air District Finds - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Eileen Vargas ,\n21 hours ago Residents living near the Chevron Richmond Refinery face a lifetime cancer risk of 37 in a million from the facility's toxic air emissions, according to a preliminary health risk assessment released by regional air regulators. That figure is more than three times higher than the Bay Area Air Quality Management District's mandatory action threshold of 10 in a million, the level at which the district requires facility-wide risk reduction plans. Read full article\n2",
